  "notes": "LA’s progressive-soul production wing — the Sa-Ra lineage that fed the West Coast jazz-rap turn. **Drums are treated as texture as much as time**: loose, dirty, deliberately unquantised, with heavy swing, an unpredictable second kick and hats crushed or replaced by noise. Harmony is modal and Sun Ra-influenced — cluster voicings, unresolved suspensions and abrupt key shifts rather than functional cycles — and the melodic lines are chromatic and wandering rather than hooky, with a dense countermelody. ⚠ **`low`**: the collective aesthetic and his role are documented, but the research says per-parameter detail is largely inferred `[LOW-CONF]`.",
